<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Arbitration Agreement</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --text: #111827;
      --muted: #4b5563;
      --border: #e5e7eb;
      --bg: #ffffff;
      --bg2: #f9fafb;
      --link: #2563eb;
    }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg2);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .wrap {
      max-width: 920px;
      margin: 32px auto;
      padding: 0 16px;
    }
    .card {
      background: var(--bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 28px;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.04);
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 4px 0;
      font-size: 22px;
      letter-spacing: .2px;
    }
    .subtitle {
      margin: 0 0 22px 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    h2 {
      margin: 22px 0 8px 0;
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    p { margin: 8px 0; }
    ul { margin: 8px 0 8px 20px; }
    li { margin: 6px 0; }
    hr {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      margin: 18px 0;
    }
    .meta {
      margin-top: 18px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--bg2);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    a { color: var(--link); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="card">
      <h1>BINDING ARBITRATION AGREEMENT</h1>
      <div class="subtitle">(AI Arbitration Platform)</div>

      <h2>1. Agreement to Arbitrate</h2>
      <p>
        By submitting a contract, accepting terms, depositing escrow funds, or otherwise using the Platform, each Party
        irrevocably agrees that any dispute arising out of or relating to the submitted contract shall be resolved
        exclusively through binding arbitration conducted via the Platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Agreement is governed by the Federal Arbitration Act (9 U.S.C. §1 et seq.).
      </p>
      <p>
        The Parties knowingly and voluntarily waive the right to litigate in court, including the right to a jury trial,
        except solely for enforcement of a Final Award.
      </p>

      <h2>2. AI Arbitrator and HITL Review</h2>
      <p>
        The Parties expressly consent to arbitration conducted by automated artificial intelligence systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Platform may use Large Language Models (LLMs), machine learning systems, and other AI tools to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review submissions</li>
        <li>Analyze evidence</li>
        <li>Interpret contractual terms</li>
        <li>Determine liability</li>
        <li>Calculate and issue awards</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A designated Human-in-the-Loop (“HITL”) reviewer may review and revert an AI determination. If reverted, the
        matter may be reassigned to the same or a different AI system for redetermination.
      </p>
      <p>
        A determination not reverted by a HITL reviewer, or a determination issued following redetermination,
        constitutes the Final Award.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Procedure</h2>
      <p>Arbitration is initiated and conducted electronically.</p>
      <p>Electronic notice to the registered email address constitutes valid and sufficient service.</p>
      <p>No in-person hearing shall be required unless mandated by applicable law.</p>
      <p>
        Texas is designated as the legal seat of arbitration, and Texas law governs to the extent not preempted by the
        Federal Arbitration Act.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Finality and Enforcement</h2>
      <p>
        The Final Award is final, binding, and enforceable. Judgment upon the Final Award may be entered in any court of
        competent jurisdiction.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Parties waive all appellate or review rights except those expressly permitted under the Federal Arbitration Act.
      </p>
      <p>Class, collective, and representative proceedings are prohibited.</p>

      <h2>5. Escrow Authority</h2>
      <p>
        If escrow funds are deposited into the designated wallet, the Parties irrevocably authorize automated distribution
        of such funds in accordance with the Final Award.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Fees</h2>
      <p>
        All administrative, filing, and processing fees are strictly non-refundable, regardless of outcome, withdrawal,
        settlement, review, or redetermination.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Electronic Consent</h2>
      <p>
        By clicking “Accept,” “Confirm,” submitting escrow funds, or otherwise indicating assent, each Party provides
        legally binding electronic consent under the U.S. E-SIGN Act and applicable Texas electronic transaction laws,
        with the same force and effect as a handwritten signature.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Severability and Survival</h2>
      <p>
        If any provision is deemed unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Arbitration Agreement survives termination of the contract and resolution of the dispute.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
